\end{equation}
Equivalently, for every $\varepsilon>0$ there exist a finite integer $p$ and
deterministic real vectors $\gamma,\beta\in\R^p$, independent of $n$ and $J$,
such that $v_p(\gamma,\beta)\ge\Pstar-\varepsilon$.
